.TH DIFF-APT-PACKAGES 1 "May 2026" "diff-apt-packages @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diff-apt-packages \- compare currently installed APT packages with default Ubuntu ones
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diff-apt-packages.sh
[\fB\-m\fR \fIMODE\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR]
[\fB\-k\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-y\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diff-apt-packages.sh
compares the set of packages currently installed on an Ubuntu system against the set of packages that come pre-installed by default for that release.
.PP
The tool determines the original package set by checking the following sources in order:
.IP "1." 4
A local manifest file specified with the \fB\-d\fR option.
.IP "2." 4
The official Ubuntu releases mirror or cloud images directory, using the automatically detected or forced system mode (\fBdesktop\fR, \fBserver\fR, \fBwsl\fR, or \fBcloud\fR).
.PP
By default, the script compares the list ignoring architecture qualifiers (e.g. \fI:amd64\fR) and normalizes version numbers in package names (e.g. treating \fIlinux-headers-6.17.0-29\fR and \fIlinux-headers-7.0.0-15\fR as the same package) to provide an accurate difference list without transient noise. Exact version matching can be re-enabled using the \fB\-k\fR option.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " MODE" ", \-\-mode " MODE
Force the installation mode to use for downloading online manifests: \fBdesktop\fR, \fBserver\fR, \fBwsl\fR, \fBcloud\fR, or \fBauto\fR. Default is \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.BI \-d " PATH" ", \-\-default-file " PATH
Specify a path to a local manifest file instead of downloading.
.TP
.BI \-o " PATH" ", \-\-output-dir " PATH
Save the parsed package lists and differences (\fIdefault-packages.txt\fR, \fIinstalled-packages.txt\fR, \fIadded-packages.txt\fR, and \fIremoved-packages.txt\fR) to the specified directory.
.TP
.B \-a\fR, \fB\-\-show-added
Print the list of added packages to standard output.
.TP
.B \-r\fR, \fB\-\-show-removed
Print the list of removed packages to standard output.
.TP
.B \-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep-versions
Do not ignore version numbers in package names. This performs exact matching on names (e.g. treating compiler releases like \fIgcc-14\fR and \fIgcc-15\fR as distinct packages).
.TP
.B \-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet
Quiet mode. Suppress all OS information headers, download progress messages, and comparison summary tables. Ideal for pipes and scripts.
.TP
.B \-y\fR, \fB\-\-non-interactive
Disable interactive prompt for listing details when run in a TTY.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show usage help summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show package difference summary and prompt for detail listings:
.PP
.RS
.B diff-apt-packages.sh
.RE
.PP
Quietly list added packages and save them to a text file:
.PP
.RS
.B diff-apt-packages.sh \-q \-a > added_packages.txt
.RE
.PP
Audit package difference comparing exact package version names:
.PP
.RS
.B diff-apt-packages.sh \-k
.RE
.PP
Force wsl mode manifest download and output raw files to a directory:
.PP
.RS
.B diff-apt-packages.sh \-m wsl \-o /tmp/wsl-audit
.RE
